    whole-table dplyr dispatch. Existing dibble typing, metadata, isolation and
    capacity rules apply. Selector helpers use qualified public tidyselect,
    rlang and base R functions. Group retention and renaming are explicit.
  Tests: public selector cases adapted into tests/testthat/test-dibble-columns.R
    from tests/testthat/test-select.R, test-rename.R and test-relocate.R,
    with Stata-typed fixtures and additional dibble ownership assertions.
  Additional Stage 2 sources:
    R/grouped-df.R: compute_groups(), dplyr_locate_sorted_groups(),
      group_data_trim(), group_intersect(), [.grouped_df
    R/rowwise.R: rowwise_df(), new_rowwise_df(), [.rowwise_df
    R/generics.R: grouped/rowwise dplyr_row_slice() and dplyr_reconstruct()
    R/arrange.R: dplyr_order_legacy(), dplyr_proxy_order_legacy()
    R/locale.R: dplyr_legacy_locale() option validation
    src/group_by.cpp: FactorExpander, VectorExpander, LeafExpander and
      grouping validation policies
  Additional destinations: R/dibble-groups.R, R/dibble-rows.R and the
    row/reconstruction hooks in R/mutate-data.R.
  Changes: factor expansion is expressed as R recursion over integer key
    positions; public vctrs grouping/slicing and tibble construction replace
    dplyr internals. Validation additionally requires a complete partition and
    matching keys before expressions run. Partition counts are linear, and
    compatible equality proxies are expanded after casting observed keys.
    Stage 7 reduces temporary allocations for ordinary integer partitions and
    uses public character match codes for classless ordinary or known-owned
    character keys. Custom classes, foreign storage and inputs with a non-NULL
    stata.storage attribute retain the general path and per-key error order.
    These are package-specific validation changes; nested capture and
    mutable-metadata checks remain.
    These use public vctrs APIs; no additional upstream source is incorporated.
    Native gathering uses the existing
    dtatools kernel. Missing strings are normalized before groups are rebuilt;
    arbitrary dataset metadata survives grouped reconstruction. The grouped
    row hook preserves its separate existing-group remapping policy. The
    legacy locale option uses base ordering of public vctrs proxies. Stage 6
    additionally adapts its lifecycle deprecation policy for arrange().
  Additional tests: tests/testthat/test-dibble-rows.R adapts group expansion,
    rowwise identifier and reconstruction cases from test-group-by.R,
    test-grouped-df.R, test-generics.R and test-rowwise.R, with package-specific
    storage, metadata, indexing and later-write isolation assertions.
    test-dibble-group-validation.R adds package-specific character equality,
    source state, foreign-length fallback and allocation regressions.
