    R/rowwise.R: rowwise.data.frame and rowwise.grouped_df
    src/chop.cpp: zero-row list/list-of prototype rule
  Destinations: R/dibble-expressions.R, R/dibble-dplyr-context.R and the
    mutate/transmute/group_by/rowwise/ungroup methods in R/mutate-data.R.
  Changes: one package-owned R evaluator replaces dplyr whole-verb evaluation.
    Column generations use isolated public handles and fixed-group bindings,
    with call-local invalidation of deferred reads. Public vctrs operations
    perform recycling and chunk assembly. Stata typing and conservative capture
    precede dependent expressions. Group metadata uses the existing module.
    Private context_env, expand_pick, expand_across and signal_warnings calls are confined to
    the optional adapter; their function bodies are not copied or patched.
    Expanded selections use full current columns; public fallback helpers use
    real dplyr against the current group. Minimum supported dplyr is 1.2.1.
  Additional tests: tests/testthat/test-dibble-expressions.R adapts helper,
    empty-group, capture and expansion cases from test-mutate.R, test-across.R,
    test-pick.R, test-group-by.R and test-rowwise.R and the standalone Stage 5
    helper proof, adding Stata sequencing and symmetric write-isolation checks.
  Additional Stage 6 sources:
    R/filter.R: filter.data.frame, check_filter, filter_rows, filter_expand
      and filter_eval policies
    R/across.R: expand_if_across integration contract
    src/filter.cpp: TRUE-only conjunction, predicate size/type validation and
      inversion after all predicates have been evaluated
    R/arrange.R: arrange.data.frame, arrange_rows, legacy proxy ordering,
      locale validation and collation
    R/locale.R: legacy-option validation and notification
    R/distinct.R: distinct.data.frame and distinct_prepare
    R/slice.R: slice.data.frame, slice_rows, slice_eval, slice_combine,
