    interfaces and row-operation methods in R/mutate-data.R.
  Changes: shared group-local evaluation plans row locations, then the existing
    package row gatherer restores typed columns, metadata and ownership.
    Arrange uses public vctrs ranks to obtain stable row permutations instead
    of private vctrs ordering. Distinct uses the shared sequential typing
    evaluator. Filter helper expansion is confined to the optional adapter;
    no installed namespace functions are patched. R evaluates and validates
    every filter predicate; an R-managed private byte buffer in C accumulates
    TRUE-only results and emits physical row locations after final inversion.
    An explicitly ungrouped plan reduces contiguous rows without materializing
    group indices; indexed groups retain row validation. The finish pass caches
    its rooted ordinary result pointer. These are package-specific changes.
    Public lifecycle and optional stringi APIs provide the
    adapted deprecation and explicit-locale policies.
