    context adapter and five methods in R/mutate-data.R.
  Changes: explicit per-group chunks retain immediate Stata typing before
    common casting and dependent dots; summary sizes are checked after all
    dots, while reframe recycles horizontally. The first assembled result is
    reused only when all recorded chunk sizes match the final group sizes;
    otherwise the existing recycling and assembly path remains.
    Typed across callbacks retain
    the observed predecessor group-major order. Public vctrs assembly and
    package gathering/finalization replace whole-verb dplyr delegation.
    Shared R/dibble-nested-capture.R is package-specific storage capture for
    nested frame/list publication, preserving public classes and intentional
    reference-valued objects rather than assuming a shallow list is isolated.
    A call-local active-node guard rejects cyclic nested list/frame payloads
    before vector assembly; completed acyclic siblings can reuse their capture.
    Its memo uses the public utils address-hash API with actual object keys and
    fixed-field source/result entries, avoiding per-address environment binding
    names. Each sibling list computes its first-identity index once.
  Additional tests: test-dibble-summary.R and test-dibble-callbacks.R adapt
    test-summarise.R, test-reframe.R, test-across.R, test-pick.R,
    test-group-map.R, test-group-nest.R and test-nest-by.R policies, with typed
    predecessor oracles and package-specific isolation/metadata regressions.
