  Resizable-vector, attribute-getter/setter/iterator, protection-stack and
  garbage-collection behavior informed the native append journal and temporary
  names placeholder. The implementation uses the public R 4.6 API. In
  particular, R_mapAttrib is experimental and confined to internal attribute
  inspection and journal roots. It neither publishes names nor changes R
  reference counts. The existing base-row adaptation above is unchanged.
  Read-loop, coercion and concatenation behavior informed owned read pointers,
  the independent ordinary snapshot passed to range, and public integer/logical
  exports through Rf_coerceVector. R's conversion implementation is called
  through its public API, not copied. No owned backing SEXP is passed to an R
  expression or returned as an untracked result.
  Interrupt-handler behavior informed portable native fault injection. The
  tests call the documented Rf_onintr entry after native writes instead of
  relying on platform C signal delivery; no interrupt implementation was copied.

