  https://svn.r-project.org/R/tags/R-4-6-1/src/main/attrib.c
  https://svn.r-project.org/R/tags/R-4-6-1/src/main/summary.c
  ALTSTRING element access, writable pointers, subset padding, encoding and
  ordinary serialization informed the extension of package-owned backing to
  characters, logicals and integer/factor columns. The module generalizes the
  package's Stage 3 implementation and uses public R APIs. Native dictionary
  descriptor pins are package-owned Rust code; no upstream implementation was
  incorporated for their lifetime management.
  Attribute-only duplication informed the internal owned-string attribute
  copy boundary, which uses the package's owned fork and Rf_setAttrib. Public
  attribute and names replacement retain R's dispatch and foreign fallbacks.
  Per-element and region read dispatch informed the native gathering and
  writer loops; no R gathering, coercion or aggregate algorithm was copied.
  Repeated subscript validation informed the qualified discrete batch route.
  Factor deep duplication and ordinary logical subset results use the package's
  copy boundary to retain ordinary R read temporaries; public classes and the
  existing fallback dispatch remain unchanged.

